//! Layer's shared setup and its sync protocol.
//!
//! The server uses these types directly. The clients get them as TypeScript,
//! generated by `bun run gen:types` into `packages/types`.
//!
//! Only what a team sets up together syncs: the repositories it works on,
//! the connections to Jira, GitHub, Slack and Grafana, the log sources
//! agents read, the models each agent offers, and repo notes. Tasks, panes,
//! runs and messages stay on the Mac that has them. So does everything that
//! is one person's own: tokens, the Jira email, Slack's notify switches, an
//! AWS profile, and where each clone is on disk.
//!
//! On the wire, field names are snake_case, the same as the database columns.

mod account;
mod agent_model;
mod connection;
mod log_source;
mod model;
mod note;
mod protocol;
mod repository;
mod user;

